# Common mistakes with the conditional functions: a condition that is not `bool`, branches of
# different types, a missing `else` value, and wrong argument counts.
mode: check
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, timestamp: datetime)
---- query
from 'orders.csv'
| project
    a = iff(qty, 1, 0),
    b = iff(amount > 100, 'big', 0),
    c = case(amount > 100, 'big', amount > 10, 'medium'),
    d = coalesce(amount, customerId),
    e = isnull(),
    f = isnotnull(amount, qty),
    g = isempty(),
    h = isnotempty(customerId, orderId)
---- expected
error[DS2006]: argument `condition` of `iff` must be `bool`, found `long`
  --> query:3:13
  |
3 |     a = iff(qty, 1, 0),
  |             ^^^ this is `long` (column `qty` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = help: to test whether it is not zero, compare it: `qty != 0`
  = note: signature: `iff(condition: bool, then: T, else: T) -> T`

error[DS2006]: argument `else` of `iff` must have the same type as argument `then` (`string`), found `long`
  --> query:4:34
  |
4 |     b = iff(amount > 100, 'big', 0),
  |                           -----  ^ this is `long`
  |                           |
  |                           this is `string`
  |
  = help: convert it first if that is what you meant: `tostring(0)`
  = note: signature: `iff(condition: bool, then: T, else: T) -> T`

error[DS2002]: `case` takes an odd number of arguments, at least 3, found 4
  --> query:5:9
  |
5 |     c = case(amount > 100, 'big', amount > 10, 'medium'),
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ called with 4 arguments
  |
  = note: signature: `case(condition: bool, value: T, ..., else: T) -> T`

error[DS2006]: the 2nd argument of `coalesce` must have the same type as the 1st argument (`real`), found `string`
  --> query:6:26
  |
6 |     d = coalesce(amount, customerId),
  |                  ------  ^^^^^^^^^^ this is `string` (column `customerId` was read from orders.csv)
  |                  |
  |                  this is `real` (column `amount` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = help: convert it first if that is what you meant: `toreal(customerId)`
  = note: signature: `coalesce(value: T, value: T, ...) -> T`

error[DS2002]: `isnull` takes 1 argument, found 0
  --> query:7:9
  |
7 |     e = isnull(),
  |         ^^^^^^^^ missing `value`
  |
  = note: signature: `isnull(value: any) -> bool`

error[DS2002]: `isnotnull` takes 1 argument, found 2
  --> query:8:27
  |
8 |     f = isnotnull(amount, qty),
  |                           ^^^ this argument is not expected
  |
  = note: signature: `isnotnull(value: any) -> bool`

error[DS2002]: `isempty` takes 1 argument, found 0
  --> query:9:9
  |
9 |     g = isempty(),
  |         ^^^^^^^^^ missing `value`
  |
  = note: signature: `isempty(value: any) -> bool`

error[DS2002]: `isnotempty` takes 1 argument, found 2
   --> query:10:32
   |
10 |     h = isnotempty(customerId, orderId)
   |                                ^^^^^^^ this argument is not expected
   |
   = note: signature: `isnotempty(value: any) -> bool`
